WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:03.630
Donald Trump has still not taken questions
from reporters.

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:04.990
It's been about a month now.

00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:10.450
It's been since before the election that we
have not actually seen Donald Trump take questions

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:12.750
from reporters yesterday.

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:18.100
Suddenly, haphazardly, a presidential press
conference was called.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.910
It was in the briefing room at the White House
and it lasted.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:23.830
This is not a mistake.

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:30.800
OK, 64 seconds, not minutes, 64 seconds is
all that.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:38.230
It was assembling the press corps for Donald
Trump to take no questions and delusional

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:41.130
brag about medical advancements.

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:46.850
And the Dow Jones Industrial Average hitting
30000 during trading yesterday.

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:48.650
Take a look at this.

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:52.410
Now, normally I say this thing went on an
hour.

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:53.640
It went on an hour and a half.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.500
I can't play the whole thing for you.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:58.540
I am playing the entire press conference for
you today.

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:00.040
OK, not a portion of it.

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:01.040
Let's start.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:02.390
Well, thank you very much.

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:05.409
And I just want to congratulate everybody.

00:01:05.409 --> 00:01:11.680
The stock market, Dow Jones Industrial Average
just hit 30000, which is the highest in history.

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:17.869
We've never broken 30000, and that's despite
everything that's taken place with the pandemic.

00:01:17.869 --> 00:01:21.630
I'm very thrilled with what's happened on
the vaccine front.

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:24.009
That's been absolutely incredible.

00:01:24.009 --> 00:01:30.259
I find it sort of hilarious that Donald Trump
comes in and says he wants to congratulate

00:01:30.259 --> 00:01:32.749
everybody, congratulate everybody for doing
what exactly?

00:01:32.749 --> 00:01:35.279
I mean, just a bizarre start.

00:01:35.279 --> 00:01:40.920
A comedy of errors, like every little detail
is hilarious and pathetic.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:45.539
That was the first 23 seconds of the 64.

00:01:45.539 --> 00:01:47.319
Let's now get to more of this.

00:01:47.319 --> 00:01:48.539
I'm showing you everything.

00:01:48.539 --> 00:01:50.749
We're going to pick it up right where we left
off.

00:01:50.749 --> 00:01:53.909
It's nothing like that has ever happened medically.

00:01:53.909 --> 00:01:58.469
And I think people are acknowledging that
and it's having a big effect.

00:01:58.469 --> 00:02:00.729
But the stock market's just broken.

00:02:00.729 --> 00:02:02.529
30000 never been broken.

00:02:02.529 --> 00:02:04.560
That number, that's a sacred number.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:05.560
Thirty thousand.

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:07.259
Nobody thought they'd ever see it.

00:02:07.259 --> 00:02:10.729
So, OK, I have to stop once more.

00:02:10.729 --> 00:02:13.890
30000 is a sacred number.

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:15.060
What?

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:20.659
What is he talking about, how is that even
a remotely sensible thing to say, it's sacred

00:02:20.659 --> 00:02:21.890
to get to 30000?

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:22.890
What?

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:25.150
I don't even know what that's supposed to
mean.

00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:28.560
And then here are the last 25 seconds.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:33.629
That's the ninth time since the beginning
of 2020.

00:02:33.629 --> 00:02:41.129
And it's the fourth time that we've broken
records in during the Trump administration.

00:02:41.129 --> 00:02:45.930
And I just want to congratulate all the people
within the administration that work so hard.

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:50.510
And most importantly, I want to congratulate
the people of our country because there are

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:51.590
no people like you.

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:53.530
Thank you very much, everybody.

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:54.870
Thank you.

00:02:54.870 --> 00:03:04.239
So that is the full press conference, 64 seconds
with Mike Pence standing behind him with this

00:03:04.239 --> 00:03:12.170
kind of Dufy smirk on his face to say congratulations
to the American people, I guess, for hitting

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:19.609
the sacred number of 30000 in the Dow Jones
Industrial Average and to claim that we've

00:03:19.609 --> 00:03:25.140
seen medical advancements like we've never
seen before thanks to his presidency and to

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:27.780
still take no questions.

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:29.329
How bizarre is this?

00:03:29.329 --> 00:03:33.620
This you know, I am I am not a person who
lacks empathy.

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:37.709
Donald Trump seems unable to experience the
feeling of empathy.

00:03:37.709 --> 00:03:39.930
I don't lack empathy.

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:50.629
And in watching these very sad 64 seconds,
I actually came close to thinking about maybe

00:03:50.629 --> 00:03:58.810
feeling slightly bad for Trump, just deflated,
grasping for anything that he can say or do

00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:01.370
to keep his grip on relevance.

00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:04.629
As the transition to Joe Biden's presidency
continues.

00:04:04.629 --> 00:04:11.190
And it seems like Trump feels that slipping
away like grant grains on a sandy beach slipping

00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:17.040
through one's fingers, it's strange to see
Donald Trump keep trying to sell himself to

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:20.320
the American people after losing an election.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:21.700
And one other funny note.

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:27.050
Back during the transition period into Trump's
administration, Donald Trump took credit for

00:04:27.050 --> 00:04:32.460
the rise in the stock market in November and
December and early January.

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:37.170
Remember, Barack Obama was still president
then, but Donald Trump took credit and said,

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:38.170
no, no.

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:41.240
Once I got elected, stocks started going up
even before I was inaugurated.

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:44.800
Thanks to me, that's the opposite of what
he's doing here.

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:51.770
He is now saying even though the stock market
is going up after Joe Biden has been elected,

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:57.290
he, as the lame duck president, still gets
credit for the stock market going up.

00:04:57.290 --> 00:05:02.710
At this point, you know, hypocrisy is dead
and double standards have no meaning with

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:04.340
this administration.

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:10.600
But just sort of like as a side note, outgoing
here, not even worth arguing with him, not

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:12.090
even worth arguing with Trump.

00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:15.030
It's about, you know, don't let the door hit
you on the way out.

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:19.640
But yet another one of these instances of
Donald Trump holding himself to a completely

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:22.250
different standard than he held Barack Obama
to.

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:24.720
And that applies to Joe Biden and that applies
to Hillary Clinton.

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:30.400
And it applies to essentially anybody that
would be seen as not friendly to Donald Trump

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:31.690
in the space of politics.

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:34.410
So he's slowly being deflated.

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:42.100
I still doubt that we will ever again see
Donald Trump do a full actual press conference

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:47.500
before leaving office where he takes questions
and he's not even going to be punished for

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:51.750
it by his followers because they will say
he's right not to take questions.

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:56.740
The media colluded with Biden and they're
all against him and they're fake.

00:05:56.740 --> 00:06:00.860
Why would he give them the ratings of letting
them ask him questions?

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:03.060
So that's what they'll say.

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:05.700
Trump will sort of fade away and he may.

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:11.290
I mean, listen, we may after Christmas, as
has been suggested, he may just leave DC and

00:06:11.290 --> 00:06:12.290
that'll be it.

00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:17.380
No appearance at the inauguration would not
be at all surprising, although for for optics

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:22.580
sake, I would be fascinated to see Donald
Trump at the inauguration of President Joseph

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:23.920
R. Biden Jr..

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:25.150
We've got a great show for you today.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:29.090
Today will be like a Friday show because it
is the last show of the week.

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:33.000
We are off tomorrow and Friday for the Thanksgiving
holiday, but we are here today.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:07:16.380
One more show and then it will be on a little
bit 

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:45.610
of 

00:07:45.610 --> 00:07:50.890
a break.

